  "title": "Refused: a batch inventory cannot feed a steady-state rate (CG-03)",
  "description": "Zielinski et al. report 224 g of wet biomass from a single 4 L batch: that is an INVENTORY. Morris et al. Example 4.1 is a STEADY-STATE control volume whose streams are RATES (kg/h). The units differ by a single character and the quantities are different things.\n\nTurning one into the other needs an operating interval. The paper states batch durations only as ranges (15-16 h, 4-5 h), which the Zielinski model deliberately refuses to collapse to a point value. Even if it were collapsed, a batch-average rate is not a steady-state one, and Morris's own schema refuses a MASS stream in a flow mode before any arithmetic happens.\n\nLoad this graph and the validation panel will show the refusal.",
  "source_ref": "Zielinski et al. (2019) sec. 4.2; Morris et al. (2011) sec. 4.5, Example 4.1",
  "notes": "Expected: one error, connection.quantity_mismatch. Do not 'fix' it by editing the unit.",
